load @term/seed/type/term
  find term

load @term/seed/type/multiplicity
  find multiplicity

# The dependent pair type, the sigma type, the one way the theory forms a type whose second component depends on its
# first. It is the existential of the foundation: a value of it is a witness paired with evidence about that witness.
# Its four rules in full.

# FORMATION: from a first type A, a multiplicity, and a second type B that may mention a variable of A, form the sigma
# type. When B ignores its variable this is the ordinary product (a pair type); when it uses it, the type of the second
# part genuinely depends on the first.
form pair-type
  link first, like term
  link usage, like multiplicity
  link second, like term

# INTRODUCTION: the pair. Given a first component of A and a second component of B at that first, the pair inhabits the
# sigma type.
form pair-introduction
  link first, like term
  link second, like term

# ELIMINATION, first projection: the first component of a pair of the sigma type inhabits A.
form first-projection
  link couple, like term

# ELIMINATION, second projection: the second component inhabits B evaluated at the first projection (the dependent
# elimination, where the type of the result depends on the first component).
form second-projection
  link couple, like term

# COMPUTATION and UNIQUENESS: projecting a pair returns its components (the beta laws fst(a, b) = a and snd(a, b) = b),
# and a pair rebuilt from its projections is the original (the eta law, surjective pairing). With observational equality
# this gives pair extensionality.
form pair-laws
  link couple, like term
